      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1362448841,
      "text": "Acacia tenuissima, commonly known as narrow-leaved wattle, broom wattle, minyana, slender mulga or slender wattle, is a shrub belonging to the genus Acacia and the subgenus Juliflorae endemic to temperate and tropical areas of Australia. Indigenous Australians, the Kurrama peoples, know the plant as Janangungu and the Banyjima know it as Murruthurru."
    },
